     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Q1-Q2 2021: 
1. Key staffing are in place. On-going recruitment of Field Coordinators (5 posts), Admin and Finance Associate, Project Assistant (2 posts).
2. Ad-hoc progress reports/regular updates for internal UNDP circulations are developed. 
3. The field missions to the targeted governorates are under planning stage. 
4. Development of ToR for TPM is underway.
5. There is no Project Board Meeting organized yet. 
6. Engagement and coordination with the government counterparts at national and governorates levels have been initiated. 7. Informal discussion have been held with potential RPs (NMO, SFCG, and others) to explain the need for a broad coalition of RPs (strengthening local support capacity), diversified approach per different regions (e.g. North and South). 

Q3 2021:
1.Key staffing are in place.
2.The development of ToR for gender specialist for the SIERY Project. The EU agreed for the project to hire a gender specialist. 
3. The project team completed field mission from 15 Aug &#x2013; 9 September 2021 to the following governorates: Aden, Lajh, Hadhramaut (both Mukalla and Seiyun), and Marib. 
The field mission covered a number of meetings with the governors of the mentioned governorates above as well as MOLA, MOPIC, district managers, responsible parties, the project facilitation and the education offices&#x2019; managers teams in each governorate on the activities and needs and how they can facilitate the implementation of the project&#x2019;s activities.
4. Third-Party Monitoring Agency (TPMA) recruited to conduct field monitoring visits.
5. No Project Board Meeting organized.
6. Conducted courtesy meetings with various local government stakeholders in IRG region including the MOLA, MOPIC, Governors as well as district managers aimed to discuss the activities and needs and how the local authorities can facilitate the implementation of the project&#x2019;s activities.
7. The selection of RPs have been initiated and expected for signing agreement with one of entity in August 2021.  

Q4 2021:
1. Completed most of the staffing recruitment, with a total of 13 staff (4 international and 9 national staff) have joined the SIERY team.
2. Signed 2 LoAs and 3 RPAs for semi-government entities as well as national NGOs to implement the project activities in the targeted areas. 
3. The TPMA has commenced their inception phase; inception report with detailing methodologies, approaches, workplan and a set of tools have been submitted to UNDP for review and clearance.
4. Monthly coordination meetings with RPs have been organized twice in 2021 with the aimed to update the progress of project, discussed challenges and possible solutions, as well as sharing best practices. 
5. Project Board Meeting is postponed until early 2022 due to donor holiday and reporting periods. 
6. Regular coordination meetings undertaken with the SIERY Technical Committee in DFA areas (2-3 times). Similarly regular updates took place in IRGY areas both at ministerial level (e.g., with MOLA), as well as with the governorate offices.</narrative>
